  "summary": {
   "status": "complete",
   "text": "In official-role posts, Oz announced AI-medical machines and other technology for Alaska health projects and said CMS is cutting red tape and leveraging AI to put patients first (s1, s3). He described harnessing data and AI as part of a shift from treating illness to preventing it and said AI can reduce paperwork and help deliver faster, smarter, more compassionate care (s2, s4). In a March 2025 statement, he said AI can free doctors and nurses from paperwork and that modernizing tools should be pursued aggressively to reduce fraud, waste, and abuse (s7, s8). In reported remarks, he said AI will be inflationary short term by turbocharging billing systems and that AI should be “out there” by the end of the administration (s9, s10).",
   "sids": [
    "s1",
    "s3",
    "s2",
    "s4",
    "s7",
    "s8",
    "s9",
    "s10"
   ],
